The prepared corpus: one Markdown file per PDF in the war.gov/ufo release, as
`graphrag-prepare` wrote it — the text layer where it was trustworthy, Tesseract
OCR where it was not, and a header on each file saying which pages went which
way. It is committed so the graph can be rebuilt with `graphrag-ingest` without
the 4 GB of PDFs or an OCR install.

Documents added through the explorer are ingested from a temporary path and are
not kept here.
